      "math_academy_id": "e-9181",
      "problem": "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\textrm{Var}[X]=3$ and $\\textrm{Var}[Y]=7.$ Find $\\textrm{Var}[X-Y].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables, then \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\textrm{Var}[X]+\\textrm{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X-Y]= 3 + 7 = 10.\n$$",
